  "limits": [
    "blocksPlaced partial batch counter and blocksBeforeSourceNeeded are absent own and parent persistent pair; fresh constructor resets partial placement count0 and threshold5. Already-set needsSource persists; partial group before that flag does not. Therefore no exact billing cadence continuity claim.",
    "setState ignores boolean world.setBlock result, then biome mutation and placement count proceed. Paid-work accounting is not conditioned on successful block write. No atomic world/source transaction.",
    "Missing radius reads0 despite constructor7. Missing tracker leaves null on fresh instance; started context can then reach tracker.computeNext and fail. No old-format fallback or field bounds validation.",
    "Spatial tracker saves absolute anchor, mirror phase and mutable cursor; saved radius/track dimensions have no consistency validation. Source availability changes do not rewrite checkpoint, but switching live relay can change getPos distance test while tracker keeps original anchor.",
    "Tile payment searches around original brazier whereas tryTick may rebind ritual.tile to relay. Exact relay lifecycle and world-dimension/native chunk persistence not runtime verified.",
    "Actual SourceUtil shortage rollback invokes current providers addSource; no transaction isolation across callbacks. Creative source returns earlier paid amounts and permits consumption-free operation intentionally. External special provider implementations not deep audited.",
    "AbstractRitual playerUUID is set onStart but not written by base/context; no actor identity continuation claim. Registry remap, unknown ritual fallback and legacy ID renames are absent.",
    "Biome helper current registry getHolderOrThrow can throw for absent configured biome; unusual vertical quart computation not tested. No guarantee full-height conversion correctness. No copied/generated architecture, no game runtime or production patch.",
    "Coordinator additionally reads actual canTakeAnotherRitual: ritual==null OR ritual.isRunning(). Thus active paid ritual can be replaced by new tablet (unchecked successful factory) without old consumedItems refund in this chain; not a paid-work conservation design. Do not invert this guard in description.",
    "ConjurePlains.read only assigns snowy biome when isSnowy true; reused instance transitioning true to false may retain snowy biome; real registry factory fresh constructor resets plains. Tracker cursor read alone is not whole ritual correctness."
